// A1 async-first seam (Stage 3): non-blocking TLS over AsyncStream (TlsStream).
//
// This closes the async-TLS gap so every DB driver can get non-blocking encrypted I/O: wolfSSL
// runs against in-memory ciphertext buffers (ALL crypto + X.509 verification stay in the audited
// library), while the record pump is Nova async over the socket — every await PARKS the coroutine
// (no scheduler thread held). A full in-process TLS handshake + encrypted round trip proves it,
// self-contained: a server coroutine (server-side wolfSSL, embedded self-signed cert) and a
// client coroutine (TlsStream) complete the handshake and exchange an encrypted PING/PONG, both
// pumped by the async scheduler. Verified under AddressSanitizer.
import assert;
import bytes;
import string;
import net.asyncio;
import net.asynctls;

// A self-signed RSA test cert + key (localhost). ONLY for this in-process loopback — the client
// connects with verify=false because it is self-signed. Real drivers use verify=true.
